Спасибо за конкретный эксперимент — он выявил реальный дефект версии `a5f7e27`. Я воспроизвёл его и переделал слой метатеории в `c2ce5a1`.

Теперь ответ на вопрос «какой тест отличает определение от декларации?» такой:

- точный вариант эксперимента заменяет **все 11 ссылок `witness`** на `DOES_NOT_EXIST`, и построение сети обязательно отклоняется: [JavaScript](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/c2ce5a10251a9a7750d6f858cb494db932c46d26/js/tests/theory-network.test.mjs#L213-L222), [Rust](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/c2ce5a10251a9a7750d6f858cb494db932c46d26/rust/tests/theory_network_tests.rs#L266-L294);
- замена всех реализаций на `DOES_NOT_EXIST` также отклоняется: [JavaScript](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/c2ce5a10251a9a7750d6f858cb494db932c46d26/js/tests/theory-network.test.mjs#L224-L233), [Rust](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/c2ce5a10251a9a7750d6f858cb494db932c46d26/rust/tests/theory_network_tests.rs#L296-L323);
- отсутствующий proof-object и proof-object от другого определения отклоняются: [JavaScript](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/c2ce5a10251a9a7750d6f858cb494db932c46d26/js/tests/theory-network.test.mjs#L235-L251), [Rust](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/c2ce5a10251a9a7750d6f858cb494db932c46d26/rust/tests/theory_network_tests.rs#L325-L348);
- предложенный эксперимент с повреждением одной предпосылки proof-object теперь тоже отклоняется именно при replay вывода: [JavaScript](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/c2ce5a10251a9a7750d6f858cb494db932c46d26/js/tests/theory-network.test.mjs#L253-L262), [Rust](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/c2ce5a10251a9a7750d6f858cb494db932c46d26/rust/tests/theory_network_tests.rs#L350-L362).

Каждый `witness` теперь содержит `implementation`, `kind` и `proof`. При загрузке проверяются точная пара implementation/kind, детерминированная исполняемая проба реализации, replay через существующий `checkProofObject` и точное совпадение проверенного заключения с `definition + subject + using + implementation + kind`: [JS validation](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/c2ce5a10251a9a7750d6f858cb494db932c46d26/js/src/rml-theory-network.mjs#L172-L368), [proof network](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/c2ce5a10251a9a7750d6f858cb494db932c46d26/lib/meta-theory/core.lino#L76-L250).

Одновременно исправлена архитектурная терминология: ambient-структура теперь `LinkNetwork`/`TheoryNetwork`, а не graph. `LinkGraph` — отдельное ограниченное подмножество с множеством вершин и типизированными по нему концами рёбер. Поверх set/type/link foundations реализованы и проверены graph reachability и relational algebra (converse, union, intersection, typed composition): [JS implementation](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/c2ce5a10251a9a7750d6f858cb494db932c46d26/js/src/rml-theory-network.mjs#L677-L843), [Rust implementation](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/c2ce5a10251a9a7750d6f858cb494db932c46d26/rust/src/theory_network.rs#L948-L1209).

Граница доверия теперь сформулирована явно: capability axioms связывают host implementation с интерпретацией; это проверяемая исполняемая реализация заявленного контракта, но не утверждение о полном доказательстве эквивалентности целых математических теорий. Также baseline исправлен с 0.0.2 на актуальный meta-theory 0.0.3 и реализованы его nested-doublet sequence/set representations.

Локально проходят 19/19 focused tests в каждом runtime, все 1239 JS tests и полный `cargo test --all-targets`. Все шесть fresh CI workflows для точного SHA `c2ce5a1` также прошли.

Implemented the quantitative foundation review in commits [`083b5e9`](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/commit/083b5e9) and [`4540584`](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/commit/4540584).

The mirrored executable report now publishes:

- total host semantic operations: **8** (six K0 operations plus two still-host-implemented derived services);
- independent primitive classification: **0 confirmed / 8 `UNKNOWN`**, using the complete `INDEPENDENT | DERIVABLE | EQUIVALENT_REENCODING | UNKNOWN` vocabulary;
- observed host/linked semantic duplication: **3** (matching, substitution, rule selection);
- self-hosting closure for the named K1 verification task: **4/11**, with all host and linked capabilities listed;
- host semantic layers: **4 bootstrap + 2 derived + 1 parsing + 1 resource control + 0 observability + 0 object-specific**;
- runtime trust coverage: **4/4 paths and 19/19 path/operation segments**, with zero undocumented paths, operations, or segments;
- foundation compression: **8/8** for the declared fault-injection probe; and
- a versioned previous/current/delta table against `e2e9f7b`.

Each of the eight operations is disabled at its real execution entry point. Every removal currently breaks the common load/import/inference/K1 probe. The report deliberately calls those results `UNKNOWN`: failure of a finite removal experiment is not presented as proof of mathematical independence or irreducibility.

The report is reproducible with `cd js && npm run report:bootstrap-metrics`; definitions and limitations are in [`bootstrap-metrics.md`](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/blob/issue-183-7fedfddffe9c/docs/case-studies/issue-183/bootstrap-metrics.md).

Verification on exact head `4540584`:

- JavaScript: **1,334/1,334** tests passed;
- Rust: **899** tests across **61** targets passed;
- all seven fresh GitHub workflows passed: tests, bootstrap, formal-corpus, parity, API docs, Docker, and lint-English;
- both npm audits report zero vulnerabilities; VS Code tests pass 4/4; formatting, syntax, and diff checks pass.

The PR title and description now contain the reproduction, metrics, limitations, test evidence, and `0.22.0` release update.

Final verification for head [`52cdcd6`](https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/commit/52cdcd6bd90e7471e4ae1e2b6ddd403b6ad5d709):

- all seven workflows triggered at `2026-09-22T01:28:20Z` completed successfully (`tests`, `docker`, `api-docs`, `bootstrap`, `formal-corpus`, `parity`, and `lint-english`);
- 10 jobs passed, the PR-only deploy job was expectedly skipped, and there are zero failing or pending checks;
- the branch is 0 commits behind `main`, local and remote head SHAs match, and GitHub reports a clean merge state;
- the worktree is clean and the PR is ready for review.

The updated description records the reproducing test, exact semantic-provenance boundary, measured before/current deltas, local verification, and the explicit limitation that S/K remain external laws rather than native Links Theory transitions.

Implemented the observation-loss follow-up from review 5780145503 in `4442b11` and documented it in `9c3a1fd`.

The new v2/v6 result keeps the binary baseline, then:

- widens the unchanged unlabelled-occurrence/equality vocabulary through widths 1–4, deriving 1/2/3/5 multiplicity classes and proving the fixed binary contract is not exhaustive outside its arity;
- marks a separate second equivalence as `CONDITIONAL_REFINEMENT_PROBE_NOT_DERIVED` / `UNESTABLISHED`, using it only to measure the forgetful projection;
- exhausts 225 width-four pairs into 33 joint classes, independently recovered by partition pairs, paired equality matrices, and intersection tables in both JavaScript and Rust;
- measures every base fibre as ambiguous (5/9/7/7/5 refinements), so the conditional observation is not recoverable from the base projection;
- derives invariant singleton occurrences in 13 classes and their absence in 20, without naming source/target or promoting automorphisms to execution; and
- publishes a provenance-aware loss audit separating intentional quotients, demonstrated loss, and properties never observed.

The candidate-table generator also has a new idempotence regression. JavaScript 1,350/1,350, all Rust targets, parity, bootstrap/report generation, docs, playground, lint, and audits pass locally. Fresh Actions on exact head `9c3a1fd16830127a9ba87ac2facc69fe5ccd0b17` pass all seven workflows. The PR now says `Advances #183`; R71, R73, and R74 remain open.

@konard, a question about reporting to link-foundation/links-notation.

Besides link-foundation/links-notation#312 and link-foundation/links-notation#313, which I filed as public issues, I found three problems in links-notation 0.20.0 that I would class as denial of service: crafted input can make parsing take a very long time or abort the process. The SECURITY.md of links-notation asks for such reports by email rather than in public issues, and private vulnerability reporting is disabled on that repository, so I have not filed them.

Could you turn on private vulnerability reporting for links-notation, or say where the details should go? This PR does not depend on a fix: the LiNo front end limits source size and nesting depth and never hands the parser the slow shapes, as the header comment of `js/src/rml-lino-frontend.mjs` explains. That comment and the experiments in this PR already show roughly which inputs are slow.
